KG42.register("rules-26f246c38f59e31ef2499f95",{"id":"19-two_stage_battery_sharing::v141-c-R007","paper":"19-two_stage_battery_sharing","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R007","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Market payment","process_stage":"settlement","market_meaning":"The ESC administers settlement by calculating individual customer energy bills and ensuring that prosumers’ income balances consumers’ expenditure. Scope: Individual customer settlement in the ESC-operated P2P sharing community. Local P2P pricing determines the electricity bills that prosumers pay or receive as repayments and that consumers pay. Scope: Electricity-bill payments and repayments of prosumers and consumers contracted with the ESC. The source states that the P2P buying-price ceiling implies lower consumer electricity bills under P2P sharing than under P2G trading. Scope: Consumer electricity bills under P2P sharing compared with P2G trading. Condition: The P2P buying price never exceeds the price of electricity bought from the grid. Under this uncompensated pricing case, the source states that prosumer income is undermined while consumers benefit; prosumers may receive less income than without P2P sharing. Scope: The source’s explanation of prosumer income and consumer benefits under uncompensated SDR pricing. Condition: The compensating price is zero and the supply-to-demand ratio exceeds one, so both P2P prices equal the grid selling price. At every studied penetration level, zero compensation is reported to leave some prosumers paying higher electricity bills or receiving lower incomes when participating in P2P sharing. Scope: The reported sensitivity evaluation across the studied penetration levels of PV battery systems. Condition: The compensating price is zero in the reported evaluation. With an appropriate compensating price, modified local SDR pricing is stated to ensure economic benefits for every individual prosumer and consumer, with economic gains described in terms of bill savings or repayments. Scope: Individual prosumer and consumer financial outcomes under modified SDR pricing compared with conventional P2G trading. Condition: The compensating price is appropriately set. Billing is conducted 24 hours after actual electricity consumption using recorded import/export energy data from smart meters, for example half-hourly records. Scope: Customer billing in the proposed two-stage P2P sharing arrangement. The positive value is the amount of electricity bill the prosumer is required to pay. Scope: Prosumer electricity-bill values in the reported financial assessment. Condition: The reported prosumer bill value is positive. The negative value denotes income received by the prosumer. Scope: Prosumer electricity-bill values in the reported financial assessment. Condition: The reported prosumer bill value is negative.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function settlement.payment under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R007-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R007-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e002","v141-b-g01-e004"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R007-E002","source":"pricing.local","target":"settlement.payment","type":"implies","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R007-C003","v141-c-R007-C004","v141-c-R007-C005","v141-c-R007-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E23","v141-b-g03-E13","v141-b-g04-E10","v141-b-g04-E15","v141-b-g04-E17"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R007-E003","source":"pricing.local","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R007-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e005","v141-b-g01-e006"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Consumer electricity bills under P2P sharing compared with P2G trading. | Customer billing in the proposed two-stage P2P sharing arrangement. | Electricity-bill payments and repayments of prosumers and consumers contracted with the ESC. | Individual customer settlement in the ESC-operated P2P sharing community. | Individual prosumer and consumer financial outcomes under modified SDR pricing compared with conventional P2G trading. | Prosumer electricity-bill values in the reported financial assessment. | The reported sensitivity evaluation across the studied penetration levels of PV battery systems. | The source’s explanation of prosumer income and consumer benefits under uncompensated SDR pricing.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e002","v141-b-g01-e004","v141-b-g01-e005","v141-b-g01-e006","v141-b-g01-e013","v141-b-g02-E23","v141-b-g03-E13","v141-b-g04-E10","v141-b-g04-E13","v141-b-g04-E15","v141-b-g04-E17"]},"x":[],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"theta_lambda_buy","symbol":"\\lambda_{buy,t}","meaning":"Price of electricity bought from the grid at time t; used in the P2G bill and the P2P buying-price ceiling.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"currency/kWh","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E07","v141-b-g03-E08","v141-b-g02-E21"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_lambda_sell","symbol":"\\lambda_{sell,t}","meaning":"Price of electricity sold to the grid at time t; used in the P2G bill, the compensating-price bound, and the uncompensated-price equality.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"currency/kWh","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E07","v141-b-g03-E08","v141-b-g02-E23"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_lambda_comp","symbol":"\\lambda","meaning":"Compensating price in the modified SDR pricing, bounded in the source by 0 \u003c= lambda \u003c= lambda_buy,t - lambda_sell,t.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"currency/kWh","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E23","v141-b-g04-E09","v141-b-g04-E10"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_P_im","symbol":"P_{im,t}^{i}","meaning":"Power imported from the grid by customer i at time t, as recorded by the individual premises smart meter for the P2G bill.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"kW","indices":["i","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E07","v141-b-g03-E08"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_P_ex","symbol":"P_{ex,t}^{i}","meaning":"Power exported to the grid by customer i at time t, as recorded by the individual premises smart meter for the P2G bill.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"kW","indices":["i","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E07","v141-b-g03-E08"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_NP","symbol":"NP_{t}^{i}","meaning":"Net-load term for customer i at time t used in the P2P bill; the source defines NP_t^i for prosumers and Eq. (36) applies the term at individual-customer level.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"kW","indices":["i","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e008","v141-b-g03-E09"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_P_aggBC","symbol":"P_{aggBC,t}^{i}","meaning":"Aggregate battery charging power term for customer i at time t entering the P2P individual bill, taken as a prior-stage/recorded settlement input.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"kW","indices":["i","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E09","v141-b-g02-E17"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_P_aggBD","symbol":"P_{aggBD,t}^{i}","meaning":"Aggregate battery discharging power term for customer i at time t entering the P2P individual bill, taken as a prior-stage/recorded settlement input.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"kW","indices":["i","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E09","v141-b-g02-E18"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_Pr_sell","symbol":"Pr_{sell}^{t}","meaning":"P2P selling price at time t from local SDR pricing, selected in the individual bill when the customer has a negative net position.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"currency/kWh","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g03-E10"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_Pr_buy","symbol":"Pr_{buy}^{t}","meaning":"P2P buying price at time t from local SDR pricing, selected in the individual bill when the customer has a positive net position.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"currency/kWh","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E22","v141-b-g03-E10"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_Pr","symbol":"Pr^{t}","meaning":"Role-dependent P2P trading price at time t used in the individual P2P bill and selected by Eq. (37).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"currency/kWh","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E09","v141-b-g03-E10"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_SDR","symbol":"SDR^{t}","meaning":"Supply-to-demand ratio at the community Microgrid at time t, used as the pricing condition for the uncompensated-price case.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"dimensionless","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E23"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_T","symbol":"T","meaning":"Number of time slots over the operation time period, used as the integral horizon in the individual bill formulas.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"time slots","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e008"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The ESC administers settlement by calculating individual customer energy bills and ensuring that prosumers’ income balances consumers’ expenditure. Scope: Individual customer settlement in the ESC-operated P2P sharing community.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e002","v141-b-g01-e004"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Local P2P pricing determines the electricity bills that prosumers pay or receive as repayments and that consumers pay. Scope: Electricity-bill payments and repayments of prosumers and consumers contracted with the ESC.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e005","v141-b-g01-e006"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C003","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"The source states that the P2P buying-price ceiling implies lower consumer electricity bills under P2P sharing than under P2G trading. Scope: Consumer electricity bills under P2P sharing compared with P2G trading. Condition: The P2P buying price never exceeds the price of electricity bought from the grid.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E13"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C004","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"Under this uncompensated pricing case, the source states that prosumer income is undermined while consumers benefit; prosumers may receive less income than without P2P sharing. Scope: The source’s explanation of prosumer income and consumer benefits under uncompensated SDR pricing. Condition: The compensating price is zero and the supply-to-demand ratio exceeds one, so both P2P prices equal the grid selling price.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E23"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C005","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"At every studied penetration level, zero compensation is reported to leave some prosumers paying higher electricity bills or receiving lower incomes when participating in P2P sharing. Scope: The reported sensitivity evaluation across the studied penetration levels of PV battery systems. Condition: The compensating price is zero in the reported evaluation.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g04-E10"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C006","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"With an appropriate compensating price, modified local SDR pricing is stated to ensure economic benefits for every individual prosumer and consumer, with economic gains described in terms of bill savings or repayments. Scope: Individual prosumer and consumer financial outcomes under modified SDR pricing compared with conventional P2G trading. Condition: The compensating price is appropriately set.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g04-E15","v141-b-g04-E17"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C007","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Billing is conducted 24 hours after actual electricity consumption using recorded import/export energy data from smart meters, for example half-hourly records. Scope: Customer billing in the proposed two-stage P2P sharing arrangement.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e013"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C008","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The positive value is the amount of electricity bill the prosumer is required to pay. Scope: Prosumer electricity-bill values in the reported financial assessment. Condition: The reported prosumer bill value is positive.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g04-E13"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C009","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The negative value denotes income received by the prosumer. Scope: Prosumer electricity-bill values in the reported financial assessment. Condition: The reported prosumer bill value is negative.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g04-E13"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C010","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"The individual P2G energy bill for customer i is the time integral over T of the grid buying price times imported power minus the grid selling price times exported power. Scope: Individual P2G settlement baseline used in the source’s comparison with P2P sharing.","expression":"BP_{2G}^{i} = \\int_{t=1}^{T} \\left( \\lambda_{buy,t} P_{im,t}^{i} - \\lambda_{sell,t} P_{ex,t}^{i} \\right) dt","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["theta_lambda_buy","theta_lambda_sell","theta_P_im","theta_P_ex","theta_T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E07","v141-b-g03-E08"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C011","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The individual P2P energy bill for customer i is the time integral over T of the customer’s net position after aggregate battery charging/discharging multiplied by the role-dependent P2P trading price. Scope: Individual customer settlement under P2P sharing.","expression":"BP_{2P}^{i} = \\int_{t=1}^{T} \\left( NP_{t}^{i} - P_{aggBC,t}^{i} + P_{aggBD,t}^{i} \\right) Pr^{t} \\, dt","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["theta_NP","theta_P_aggBC","theta_P_aggBD","theta_Pr","theta_T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E09"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C012","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The P2P trading price used in the individual bill is the P2P selling price when the customer’s net position after aggregate battery charging/discharging is negative and the P2P buying price when that net position is positive. Scope: Role-dependent P2P price selection in individual settlement. The source does not print a case for a zero net position.","expression":"Pr^{t} = \\begin{cases} Pr_{sell}^{t}, & NP_{t}^{i} - P_{aggBC,t}^{i} + P_{aggBD,t}^{i} \u003c 0 \\\\ Pr_{buy}^{t}, & NP_{t}^{i} - P_{aggBC,t}^{i} + P_{aggBD,t}^{i} > 0 \\end{cases}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["theta_Pr","theta_Pr_sell","theta_Pr_buy","theta_NP","theta_P_aggBC","theta_P_aggBD"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E09","v141-b-g03-E10"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C013","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"When the compensating price is zero and the supply-to-demand ratio exceeds one, both P2P selling and buying prices equal the grid selling price. Scope: Price consequence under uncompensated SDR pricing. This formalizes the price-equality part of the source’s uncompensated-pricing statement; the associated income and consumer-benefit conclusions remain qualitative.","expression":"(\\lambda = 0 \\land SDR^{t} > 1) \\Rightarrow \\left( Pr_{sell}^{t} = Pr_{buy}^{t} = \\lambda_{sell,t} \\right)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["theta_lambda_comp","theta_SDR","theta_Pr_sell","theta_Pr_buy","theta_lambda_sell"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E23"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C014","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"For a consumer with no export, if the P2P buying price never exceeds the grid buying price at each time, the consumer’s P2P energy bill is lower than the P2G bill. Scope: Consumer bill comparison under the P2P buying-price ceiling.","expression":"\\left( \\forall t,\\; Pr_{buy}^{t} \\le \\lambda_{buy,t} \\right) \\land \\left( \\forall t,\\; P_{ex,t}^{i} = 0 \\right) \\Rightarrow BP_{2P}^{i} \u003c BP_{2G}^{i}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["theta_Pr_buy","theta_lambda_buy","theta_P_ex"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E13","v141-b-g03-E08"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e002","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":"264","section":"2.1. P2P energy sharing structure","anchor_text":"surplus PV power from prosumers can also be traded with consumers who do not have PV systems. PP A t","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"A third party entity named “energy sharing coordinator (ESC)” coordinates between customers and provides P2P sharing services, i.e. assuring the power balance and payment balance [13]. The ESC is the controller of the DERs as well as the local market operator. The ESC is located at the PCC (e.g. the low voltage substation). A smart meter is installed at the PCC, measuring the real-time net power consumption of the community, and this measurement is the input of the ESC. The ESC is communicated with the controllers of these small-scale batteries at the prosumer premises, and provides control signals to them via one-way communication. Through managing the battery charging/discharging, the ESC ensures the maximum use of local energy resources and the minimum amount of electricity fed back into the grid. Therefore the overall energy cost of the community is reduced, and the reduced cost is distributed to individual customers through a P2P pricing mechanism. The ESC also calculates energy bills of individual customers based on the P2P pricing mechanism, using the recorded import/export energy (e.g. half-hourly) from smart meters at the premises."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e004","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":"264","section":"2.1. P2P energy sharing structure","anchor_text":"Details of the control framework and the pricing mechanism for the local market are presented in Sec","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"(1) Energy sharing coordinator (ESC)\n• Export power to (or import power from) the main grid to ensure the power balance of the community;\n• Contract with a supplier for the electricity trade at pre-defined exporting/importing prices and ensure the payment balance between the community and the supplier;\n• Control the charging/discharging activities of all batteries;\n• Contract with individual prosumers and consumers according to the P2P pricing mechanism and ensure the prosumers’ income balance with the consumers’ expenditure."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e005","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p04-c2r1__v141-a-M01-participation","page":4,"printed_page":"264","section":"2.1. P2P energy sharing structure","anchor_text":"Applied Energy 226 (2018) 261–276 the power balance of the community; Contract with a supplier for t","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"(2) Prosumers\n• Hand over the control of their batteries to the ESC;\n• Contract with the ESC, pay/repay their electricity bills according to the P2P pricing mechanism (The prices are calculated 24 h after the actual consumption according to the predefined pricing mechanism)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e006","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":4,"printed_page":"264","section":"2.1. P2P energy sharing structure","anchor_text":"p g ( p he after the actual consumption according to the predeﬁned pricing is mechanism). (3) Consum","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"(3) Consumers\n• Contract with the ESC, pay their electricity bill according to the P2P pricing mechanism (The prices are calculated 24 h after the actual consumption according to the predefined pricing mechanism)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e013","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":3,"printed_page":"263","section":"1. Introduction","anchor_text":"in munity point of view, e.g. [19]. A thorough assessment method is ﬀ required to analyze the beneﬁt","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"restatement"},"source_text":"A novel two-stage aggregated control framework was proposed to realize P2P energy sharing in low voltage distribution networks. Comparing to the previous works of P2P energy sharing with a third party entity, this control framework requires for very limited measurements and a one-way communication, providing a feasible and practical solution to P2P energy sharing. Compared to the P2P energy sharing without an intermedia, there is no need of fast communication between the market operator and the individual DERs, because the pricing and billing are conducted 24 h after the actual electricity consumption, using the recorded import/export energy (e.g. half-hourly) data from smart meters. Also, there are no divergence issues."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E23","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p08-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"prices would dynamically change according to Eqs. (19) and (20). The relation of the P2P buying/sell","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"When SDR^{t} = 0, there is no selling power in the community, and all the required energy is bought from the main grid. The P2P selling and buying prices are both equal to the price of electricity bought from the grid (i.e. Pr_{sell}^{t} = Pr_{buy}^{t} = \\lambda_{buy,t}). When SDR^{t} = 1, the selling power is equal to the buying power in the community, and no power is required to import from (or export to) the main grid. The P2P selling and buying prices are both equal to the price of electricity sold to the grid with a compensation (i.e. Pr_{sell}^{t} = Pr_{buy}^{t} = \\lambda_{sell,t} + \\lambda). Here, \\lambda is a compensating price (0 \\le \\lambda \\le \\lambda_{buy,t} - \\lambda_{sell,t}), and it is used to compensate the prosumers to ensure the prosumers be better off when they participate in P2P energy sharing. When 0 \u003c SDR^{t} \u003c 1, or SDR^{t} > 1, the P2P selling and buying prices would dynamically change according to Eqs. (19) and (20). The reason for introducing the compensating price is that, when there is no compensating price (i.e. \\lambda = 0), both P2P selling and buying prices are equal to the price of electricity sold to grid when the SDR is more than 1. This will undermine the prosumers' income, but provide economic benefits to the consumers (i.e. these who do not have PV battery systems). It might happen that the prosumers receive lower incomes than the case of not participating in P2P energy sharing."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E13","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p11-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":11,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"sharing than under the P2G energy trading. Hence, there is no need to ti evaluate the participation ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-11.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"For the consumers, as the P2P buying price (Pr_{buy}^t) is never higher than the price of electricity bought from the grid (\\lambda_{buy,t}), the energy bill of consumers will be always lower when participating in P2P energy sharing than under the P2G energy trading. Hence, there is no need to evaluate the participation willingness of consumers."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E10","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p14-c1r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":14,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"battery, but it only requires to reduce the price of the battery system to ev £430/kWh (only 14% low","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-14.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"When the compensating price is zero, at all the penetration levels of PV battery systems, some prosumers are paying more electricity bills or gaining lower incomes when participating in P2P energy sharing. This is because the economic beneﬁts were obtained by the consumers, whilst for some of the prosumers, it may not be worth participating in P2P energy sharing."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E13","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p14-c2r1__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":14,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Applied Energy 226 (2018) 261–276 f- means the amount of income the prosumer receives. It is found t","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-14.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"For the prosumers, a positive value means the amount of electricity bill the prosumer is required to pay, and a negative value means the amount of income the prosumer receives."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E15","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p15-c1r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":15,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"pr This paper proposed a two-stage control method to realize P2P energy sharing in community Microgr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-15.png","occurrence_role":"restatement"},"source_text":"With an appropriate setting of the compensating price, the modiﬁed supply demand ratio based mechanism ensures every individual customer in the community be better oﬀcompared to the conventional P2G energy trading, i.e. every individual prosumer and consumer gain economic beneﬁts. This pricing mechanism can be used as a benchmark applicable to any P2P energy sharing model."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p14-c2r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":14,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"to evolutionary algorithms to achieve the global optimum for P2P energy sharing is considered as one","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-14.png","occurrence_role":"exception"},"source_text":"The unfairness of economic gains may exist, i.e. there are diﬀerences in bill savings (or repayments) among consumers (or prosumers)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e008","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":"264","section":"2.2. Modelling of load and photovoltaic systems","anchor_text":"p g ( p he after the actual consumption according to the predeﬁned pricing is mechanism). (3) Consum","equation_id":"1-3","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"P_{L}^{i} \\triangleq [P_{L,1}^{i}, P_{L,2}^{i}, \\ldots, P_{L,T}^{i}], \\quad i \\in [1, 2, \\ldots, N] \\qquad (1)\nwhere N is the total number of customers. T is the number of time slots over the operation time period. The PV generation of the PV battery system at the ith customer premises (these customers are also prosumers) is defined as\nP_{PV}^{i} \\triangleq [P_{PV,1}^{i}, P_{PV,2}^{i}, \\ldots, P_{PV,T}^{i}], \\quad i \\in [1, 2, \\ldots, NB] \\qquad (2)\nwhere NB is the total number of prosumers (NB \\leqslant N). For the ith prosumer, the net load at the time t is presented by\nNP_{t}^{i} = P_{L,t}^{i} - P_{PV,t}^{i} \\qquad (3)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p08-c1r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"C. Long et al. N of ⎧ − ∑ NPti N NB ⎪ i = 1 i i i i ⎪ NB ∗ PBC , max − ∑ NPt \u003c ∑ PBC , max & SOCt P ","equation_id":"(13)-(14)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"P_{aggBC,t}^{i} = \\begin{cases} \\frac{-\\sum_{i=1}^{N} NP_{t}^{i}}{\\sum_{i=1}^{NB} P_{BC,max}^{i}} * P_{BC,max}^{i}, & -\\sum_{i=1}^{N} NP_{t}^{i} \u003c \\sum_{i=1}^{NB} P_{BC,max}^{i} \\text{ and } SOC_{t}^{i} \u003c SOC_{max}^{i} \\\\ P_{BC,max}^{i}, & -\\sum_{i=1}^{N} NP_{t}^{i} \\ge \\sum_{i=1}^{NB} P_{BC,max}^{i} \\text{ and } SOC_{t}^{i} \u003c SOC_{max}^{i} \\\\ 0, & SOC_{t}^{i} = SOC_{max}^{i} \\end{cases} \\quad P_{aggBD,t}^{i}=0 \\quad (13) The control set-point has to be within the upper and lower limits of the boundary, and this is presented by P_{aggBC,t}^{i} = \\begin{cases} x_{t}^{i} - \\frac{\\Delta P_{BW}}{2}, & \\text{if } P_{aggBC,t}^{i} \u003c x_{t}^{i} - \\frac{\\Delta P_{BW}}{2} \\\\ x_{t}^{i} + \\frac{\\Delta P_{BW}}{2}, & \\text{if } P_{aggBC,t}^{i} > x_{t}^{i} + \\frac{\\Delta P_{BW}}{2} \\end{cases} \\quad (14)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E18","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p08-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"⎧ ∑ NPti NB pr ⎪ i = 1 i N i i i re ⎪ NB ∗ PBD, max ∑i = 1 NPt \u003c ∑ PBC , max & SOCt sh ⎪ ∑ PBDi , ma","equation_id":"(15)-(16)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"P_{BC,t}^{i}=0; P_{aggBD,t}^{i} = \\begin{cases} \\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^{N} NP_{t}^{i}}{\\sum_{i=1}^{NB} P_{BD,max}^{i}} * P_{BD,max}^{i}, & \\sum_{i=1}^{N} NP_{t}^{i} \u003c \\sum_{i=1}^{NB} P_{BC,max}^{i} \\text{ and } SOC_{t}^{i} > SOC_{min}^{i} \\\\ P_{BD,max}^{i}, & \\sum_{i=1}^{N} NP_{t}^{i} \\ge \\sum_{i=1}^{NB} P_{BC,max}^{i} \\text{ and } SOC_{t}^{i} > SOC_{min}^{i} \\\\ 0, & SOC_{t}^{i} = SOC_{min}^{i} \\end{cases} \\quad (15) The control set-point has to be within the upper and lower limits of the boundary, and this is presented by P_{aggBD,t}^{i} = \\begin{cases} x_{t}^{i} - \\frac{\\Delta P_{BW}}{2}, & \\text{if } P_{aggBD,t}^{i} \u003c x_{t}^{i} - \\frac{\\Delta P_{BW}}{2} \\\\ x_{t}^{i} + \\frac{\\Delta P_{BW}}{2}, & \\text{if } P_{aggBD,t}^{i} > x_{t}^{i} + \\frac{\\Delta P_{BW}}{2} \\end{cases} \\quad (16)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E19","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p08-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"3.3. P2P trading mechanism Given the fact that in economics the relation between price and SDR is in","equation_id":"(17)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Given the fact that in economics the relation between price and SDR is inverse-proportional, reference [13] formulated a P2P pricing model based on the supply and demand ratio. Here, the SDR method is also used. The total selling power is from the PV battery systems, which is equal to the remaining PV power after carrying out the charging or discharging activities, and the total buying power is the customer demand. Thus, the SDR at a community Microgrid at time t is defined as, SDR^{t} = \\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^{NB} (P_{PV,t}^{i} - P_{aggBC,t}^{i} + P_{aggBD,t}^{i})}{\\sum_{i=1}^{N} P_{L,t}^{i}} \\quad (17)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E20","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p08-c2r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Applied Energy 226 (2018) 261–276 of the day, and the price set is presented by Pr = {Prbuy1 , Prbuy","equation_id":"(18)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"of the day, and the price set is presented by \\mathbf{Pr} = \\{Pr_{buy}^{1}, Pr_{buy}^{2}, \\dots, Pr_{buy}^{t}, \\dots, Pr_{buy}^{T}; Pr_{sell}^{1}, Pr_{sell}^{2}, \\dots, Pr_{sell}^{t}, \\dots, Pr_{sell}^{T}\\} \\quad (18) where Pr_{buy}^{t} is the P2P buying price at time t, and Pr_{sell}^{t} is the P2P selling price at time t."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E21","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p08-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"λ ( λ sell t + )·λbuy , , t3) 0 ⩽ SDRt ⩽ 1 ⎧ SDR − t + λ )· sell (λ buy , t − λ , t λ sell , t + λ t","equation_id":"(19)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The P2P buying price (Pr_{buy}^{t}) should not be higher than the price of electricity bought from the grid (\\lambda_{buy,t}) and the P2P selling price (Pr_{sell}^{t}) should not be lower than the price of electricity sold to the grid (\\lambda_{sell,t}). Therefore, the P2P selling and buying prices are defined as a function of the SDR. They are shown as Pr_{sell}^{t} = f(SDR^{t}) = \\begin{cases} \\frac{(\\lambda_{sell,t} + \\lambda)\\lambda_{buy,t}}{(\\lambda_{buy,t} - \\lambda_{sell,t} - \\lambda)SDR^{t} + \\lambda_{sell,t} + \\lambda}, & 0 \\le SDR^{t} \\le 1 \\\\ \\lambda_{sell,t} + \\frac{\\lambda}{SDR^{t}}, & SDR^{t} > 1 \\end{cases} \\quad (19)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E22","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p08-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"λ ( λ sell t + )·λbuy , , t3) 0 ⩽ SDRt ⩽ 1 ⎧ SDR − t + λ )· sell (λ buy , t − λ , t λ sell , t + λ t","equation_id":"(20)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Pr_{buy}^{t} = f'(SDR^{t}) = \\begin{cases} Pr_{sell}^{t} \\cdot SDR^{t} + \\lambda_{buy,t} \\cdot (1 - SDR^{t}), & 0 \\le SDR^{t} \\le 1 \\\\ \\lambda_{sell,t} + \\lambda, & SDR^{t} > 1 \\end{cases} \\quad (20)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E07","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p09-c2r4__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"buy , t ∗ Pim , t λ sell , t ∗ Pex , t ) dt (35) BP 2G = ∫t = 1 (λ 7) Power PPV ty PM EBC PL 8) EBD ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The cost of energy for individual premises with P2G trading is calculated by BP_{2G}^i = \\int_{t=1}^{T} (\\lambda_{buy,t} * P_{im,t}^i - \\lambda_{sell,t} * P_{ex,t}^i) dt \\tag{35}."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E08","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p10-c1r1__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":10,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"C. Long et al. where BPi 2G is the energy bill for customer i under P2G energy trading. i positive.F","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-10.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"For consumers, P_{ex,t}^i is equal to zero, therefore BP_{2G}^i is always positive. For prosumers, BP_{2G}^i can be positive or negative. When BP_{2G}^i is positive, this means this is the amount of electricity bill the customer needs to pay. When BP_{2G}^i is negative, this means this is the amount of income the customer will be repaid."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p10-c1r1__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":10,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"C. Long et al. where BPi 2G is the energy bill for customer i under P2G energy trading. i positive.F","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-10.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The cost of energy for individual customers with P2P energy sharing is calculated by BP_{2P}^i = \\int_{t=1}^{T} [(NP_t^i - P_{aggBC,t}^i + P_{aggBD,t}^i) \\cdot Pr^t] dt \\tag{36}; where BP_{2P}^i is the energy bill for customer i under P2P energy sharing. Pr^t is the P2P trading price, and the value of the Pr^t depends on the role (i.e. consumer or producer) the customer is playing at time t."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E10","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p10-c2r1__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":10,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Applied Energy 226 (2018) 261–276 g. ⎧ Prsellt , NPti −PaggBCi , t + PaggBDi , t \u003c 0 e. t ⎪ Pr = 0 ,","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-10.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Therefore, Pr^t is calculated by Pr^t = \\left\\{ \\begin{array}{ll} Pr_{sell}^t, & NP_t^i - P_{aggBC,t}^i + P_{aggBD,t}^i \u003c 0 \\\\ Pr_{buy}^t, & NP_t^i - P_{aggBC,t}^i + P_{aggBD,t}^i > 0 \\end{array} \\right. \\tag{37}"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p14-c1r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":14,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"battery, but it only requires to reduce the price of the battery system to ev £430/kWh (only 14% low","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-14.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"It is found that with a higher compensating price, it is ensured 100% of the participation willingness, i.e. every prosumer is better oﬀwhen participating in P2P energy sharing compared to the P2G energy trading."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"The settlement rule does not select a design or operational decision variable. The supported formulas contain metered data, prior-stage battery/price outcomes, and exogenous prices, which are represented as theta inputs rather than x decisions.","empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-pricing","v141-a-M01-settlement"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e002","quote":"The ESC also calculates energy bills of individual customers based on the P2P pricing mechanism, using the recorded import/export energy (e.g. half-hourly) from smart meters at the premises."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e004","quote":"Contract with individual prosumers and consumers according to the P2P pricing mechanism and ensure the prosumers’ income balance with the consumers’ expenditure."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e005","quote":"Contract with the ESC, pay/repay their electricity bills according to the P2P pricing mechanism"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e006","quote":"Contract with the ESC, pay their electricity bill according to the P2P pricing mechanism"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E13","quote":"For the consumers, as the P2P buying price (Pr_{buy}^t) is never higher than the price of electricity bought from the grid (\\lambda_{buy,t}), the energy bill of consumers will be always lower when participating in P2P energy sharing than under the P2G energy trading."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E23","quote":"when there is no compensating price (i.e. \\lambda = 0), both P2P selling and buying prices are equal to the price of electricity sold to grid when the SDR is more than 1. This will undermine the prosumers' income, but provide economic benefits to the consumers (i.e. these who do not have PV battery systems). It might happen that the prosumers receive lower incomes than the case of not participating in P2P energy sharing."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E10","quote":"When the compensating price is zero, at all the penetration levels of PV battery systems, some prosumers are paying more electricity bills or gaining lower incomes when participating in P2P energy sharing."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E15","quote":"With an appropriate setting of the compensating price, the modiﬁed supply demand ratio based mechanism ensures every individual customer in the community be better oﬀcompared to the conventional P2G energy trading, i.e. every individual prosumer and consumer gain economic beneﬁts."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E17","quote":"The unfairness of economic gains may exist, i.e. there are diﬀerences in bill savings (or repayments) among consumers (or prosumers)."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e013","quote":"the pricing and billing are conducted 24 h after the actual electricity consumption, using the recorded import/export energy (e.g. half-hourly) data from smart meters."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E13","quote":"For the prosumers, a positive value means the amount of electricity bill the prosumer is required to pay, and a negative value means the amount of income the prosumer receives."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E13","quote":"For the prosumers, a positive value means the amount of electricity bill the prosumer is required to pay, and a negative value means the amount of income the prosumer receives."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"644d77d154b9c7b7d7b104633b0e7b5fb2e9588f993afc664ee38103ef3e82c8","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The settlement rule has directly supported source formulas: the individual P2G bill Eq. (35), the individual P2P bill Eq. (36), the role-dependent P2P price selection Eq. (37), and the explicit zero-compensation price equality. These are formalized at settlement.payment, with pricing.local where local P2P prices enter. The remaining C.1 statements are qualitative comparative claims, reported evaluation outcomes, or procedural billing requirements and are left not_formalized rather than forced into unsupported equations. B evidence remains UNREVIEWED and is used here only as eligible provisional source support, not as independently verified source correctness.","bindings":[{"object_id":"theta_lambda_buy","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E002"],"rationale":"lambda_buy,t is the grid purchase price used in the P2P buying-price ceiling and the P2G bill; E002 carries the pricing-to-settlement implication for the price comparisons."},{"object_id":"theta_lambda_sell","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E002"],"rationale":"lambda_sell,t is the grid sale price used in the compensating-price bound and the uncompensated-price equality; E002 is the pricing-to-settlement edge associated with C004."},{"object_id":"theta_lambda_comp","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E002"],"rationale":"lambda is the compensating price in C004 and C006; E002 links local pricing conditions to settlement outcomes."},{"object_id":"theta_P_im","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"P_im,t^i is a metered import quantity in the P2G bill Eq. (35); it is a settlement input and does not require a pricing edge."},{"object_id":"theta_P_ex","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"P_ex,t^i is a metered export quantity in the P2G bill Eq. (35); it is a settlement input and does not require a pricing edge."},{"object_id":"theta_NP","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"NP_t^i enters the individual P2P bill Eq. (36) as a recorded or prior-stage net-load term at settlement."},{"object_id":"theta_P_aggBC","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"P_aggBC,t^i enters the individual P2P bill Eq. (36) as a prior-stage aggregate battery charging term."},{"object_id":"theta_P_aggBD","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"P_aggBD,t^i enters the individual P2P bill Eq. (36) as a prior-stage aggregate battery discharging term."},{"object_id":"theta_Pr_sell","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E003"],"rationale":"Pr_sell^t is a local P2P price selected in Eq. (37) and used in the settlement bill; E003 links local P2P pricing to settlement.payment."},{"object_id":"theta_Pr_buy","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E003"],"rationale":"Pr_buy^t is a local P2P price selected in Eq. (37) and used in the settlement bill; E003 links local P2P pricing to settlement.payment."},{"object_id":"theta_Pr","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E003"],"rationale":"Pr^t is the role-dependent local P2P price in the individual bill; E003 captures local P2P pricing determining bills."},{"object_id":"theta_SDR","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"SDR^t is a pricing.local condition used to characterize the zero-compensation price case; it has no separate edge in this settlement rule."},{"object_id":"theta_T","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"T is the integral time horizon in the individual bill formulas at settlement.payment."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C010","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Eq. (35) is a settlement accounting identity using grid prices and metered import/export; it is the P2G baseline and does not use pricing.local."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C011","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E003"],"rationale":"Eq. (36) uses the role-dependent P2P price from pricing.local in the individual settlement bill; E003 is the pricing-to-settlement link."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C012","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E003"],"rationale":"Eq. (37) selects Pr_sell or Pr_buy for the settlement bill; E003 captures local P2P pricing determining bills."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C013","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E002"],"rationale":"The lambda=0 and SDR>1 price equality is part of the uncompensated pricing condition in C004; E002 is the corresponding pricing-to-settlement edge."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C014","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E002"],"rationale":"This formalizes C003’s consumer bill comparison under the P2P buying-price cap; E002 is the pricing-to-settlement implication edge for the price comparisons."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
